<title>UK: General Accident eases as UBS repeats sell.</title>
<headline>General Accident eases as UBS repeats sell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in  General Accident Plc eased on Thursday as brokerage UBS repeated a &quot;sell&quot; recommendation, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1030 GMT, the shares were off 8p to 833-1/2, having slipped as low as 829-3/4 earlier.</p>
<p>UBS said it believes the shares are overvalued by about 15 percent.</p>
<p>The brokerage's comments, coupled with a generally weak market, dragged the shares lower, dealers said. However, they noted that selling was not particularly heavy. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
